Oxlint 1.89.0 and 1.90.0 report `unicorn/require-post-message-target-origin` for native messaging APIs that do not accept a Window target origin, and suggest properties or argument types those receivers do not support.

### Reproduction

`main.js`:

```js
const channel = new BroadcastChannel('example');
channel.postMessage({ type: 'ping' });
const worker = new Worker(new URL('./worker.js', import.meta.url), { type: 'module' });
worker.postMessage({ type: 'ping' });
window.postMessage({ type: 'ping' });
```

`worker.js` (loaded as a dedicated worker by `main.js`):

```js
self.onmessage = () => {
  self.postMessage({ type: 'pong' });
};
```

`oxlint.json`:

```json
{"plugins":["unicorn"],"rules":{"unicorn/require-post-message-target-origin":"warn"}}
```

Run with Oxlint 1.89.0 or 1.90.0:

```sh
oxlint --config oxlint.json --allow all --warn unicorn/require-post-message-target-origin main.js worker.js
```

### Actual result

All four calls are reported. The suggestions insert `channel.location.origin`, `worker.location.origin`, `window.location.origin`, and `self.location.origin`, respectively.

`BroadcastChannel` and the `Worker` instance have no `location` property. In the dedicated worker, `self.location.origin` exists, but a string origin is not the second argument accepted by its `postMessage` overloads. Following these suggestions can turn valid messaging calls into runtime errors.

### Expected result

Keep reporting the `Window.postMessage` control case, while avoiding Window-origin diagnostics and suggestions for the non-Window APIs. The two constructor-bound receivers provide local evidence of their API without needing to infer an arbitrary receiver. If the worker-global case cannot be distinguished, avoiding the invalid origin suggestion would still help.

API references: [BroadcastChannel.postMessage](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/BroadcastChannel/postMessage), [Worker.postMessage](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Worker/postMessage), and [DedicatedWorkerGlobalScope.postMessage](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/DedicatedWorkerGlobalScope/postMessage).

Related history: [Unicorn #1396](https://github.com/sindresorhus/eslint-plugin-unicorn/issues/1396) is closed. The [current Unicorn rule documentation](https://github.com/sindresorhus/eslint-plugin-unicorn/blob/main/docs/rules/require-post-message-target-origin.md) acknowledges receiver ambiguity. This report concerns the reproducible Oxlint diagnostics and invalid suggestions for these native APIs.

